---
description: Delegate /mycodex tasks to the local Codex CLI; receipts are not completed work.
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user invokes `/mycodex:run`, `/mycodex:review`, `/mycodex:setup`, `/mycodex:status`, `/mycodex:result`, or `/mycodex:cancel`:

- Call the MyCodex companion (`scripts/codex-run.mjs`) via Shell. Do not implement the coding task yourself.
- A JSON receipt (`kind: "receipt"`) means the job started. It is not the finished result.
- Do not add `--model` or `--effort` unless the user wrote them.
- Do not run `codex exec resume --last`.
- A write job owns the files it is changing; do not edit those files in parallel.
- Review is read-only and may run beside a write job. Do not treat review findings as applied changes.
